scaffold_prompt:
Create a scaffold for an original short story. Do not write the story yet.

You may choose any genre, cast size, setting, and scene structure.

Your scaffold must include:
- title;
- genre / mode;
- one-sentence premise;
- main character(s), with motives and constraints;
- setting / world rules if relevant;
- central conflict;
- emotional or thematic pressure;
- 5–8 major story beats in order;
- at least two details planted early that should pay off later;
- intended ending shape;
- prose style / register target;
- what must not change during drafting.

Keep the scaffold concise, concrete, and operational. Do not write scene prose yet.
